PixelU-Wii patch for Bochs' disassembler (svn r12420), opcodes.inc.

"adc r/m64, imm32" (REX.W 81 /2 id) takes a sign-extended 32-bit immediate,
like add, or, sbb, and, sub, xor and cmp in the same table. The r12420 table
gives it a 64-bit immediate (Iq), so the disassembler reads four bytes too
many and every instruction after it in the JIT's host-code view is wrong.
This changes the operand to sIdq, the one its seven siblings use.

--- a/bochs/disasm/opcodes.inc
+++ b/bochs/disasm/opcodes.inc
@@ -38,3 +38,3 @@
 Ia_adcq_Eq_sIb = { "adc", "adcq", Eq, sIbq, XX, XX, 0 },
-Ia_adcq_Eq_sId = { "adc", "adcq", Eq, Iq, XX, XX, 0 },
+Ia_adcq_Eq_sId = { "adc", "adcq", Eq, sIdq, XX, XX, 0 },
 Ia_adcq_Gq_Eq = { "adc", "adcq", Gq, Eq, XX, XX, 0 },
